### Quickstart — the two cases the assignment brief names.
# Run `docker compose up -d` first and wait for /health to report UP.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiKey = dev-only-insecure-key-do-not-use-in-production-env

### Health — no API key required. Expect 200 {"status":"UP"}.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Case 1: a company name in an email address finds the client.
# "NevisWealth" matches john.doe@neviswealth.com through pg_trgm word_similarity,
# which splits the address into john / doe / neviswealth / com. Expect John Doe
# first, with match.field = email and match.tier = identity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=NevisWealth&limit=5
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Case 2: a KYC category finds documents that never use the word.
# "address proof" returns utility bills, council tax bills, bank statements and
# tenancy agreements. Each result reports which signals admitted it:
#   label    — the document is tagged proof_of_address
#   lexical  — the words matched a tsvector
#   semantic — the embedding matched, no shared words needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=address%20proof&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### The same question in the wording the brief uses. Same answers.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=proof%20of%20address&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### "utility bill" as a category. Zero clients, despite a client named Bill Carter.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=utility%20bill&limit=10
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Interactive API docs, served without a key.
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui.html

### The generated OpenAPI document.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs
